<BaseLayout title="About us" description="Learn about Back2School Africa, an education-focused NPO connecting learning, skills development and community.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap narrow"><span class="eyebrow">About Back2School Africa</span><h1>Education is a way forward.</h1><p class="lead">Back2School Africa is an education-focused NPO working across learning, skills development and community connection.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap two-col"><div><span class="eyebrow">Our purpose</span><h2>Restoring dignity through education.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Learning matters at every stage of life. A reading club can help a child build confidence. Tutoring can make a difficult subject more approachable. Guidance can help a young person see and prepare for the choices ahead.</p><p>Our programme areas bring those steps together: skills development, career guidance, tutoring, reading clubs, university applications and mentoring.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programmes/">Explore the programmes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
  <figure class="about-photo wrap"><img src="/images/joburg-library-learning.webp" width="634" height="615" loading="lazy" alt="Children learning together with a tablet at a Johannesburg library" /><figcaption>Community learning at a Johannesburg library. Photo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CHILDREN_USING_TABLETS_TO_PLAY_GAMES_AND_AND_READ_STORIES_AT_RABBI_RIDGE_LIBRARYJOBURG_SOUTH_AFRICA.jpg">JeffNyoka / Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Cropped and converted to WebP. This is not a Back2School Africa programme photo.</figcaption></figure>
  <section class="section wash" id="approach"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">How we think about support</span><div class="principle-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Start where people are</h3><p>Make it easier to find a relevant entry point, whether the need is reading practice, subject support or future planning.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Connect the next steps</h3><p>Learning, skills and opportunity are related. Our programmes reflect the journey rather than a single moment.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Grow with community</h3><p>Tutors, mentors, families, volunteers and partners all have a role in opening pathways.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap editorial-callout"><h2>Want to be part of the journey?</h2><p>Find a path to participate or start a conversation with the team.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/get-involved/">Get involved <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Contact us <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
